{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The fifth time</b><br>Shesh. Marble." "<b>The third time</b><br>His thighs. [It is] fire and air." "Upon adonim of paz. It is the earth, like 'concerning what (על מה) its adonim were fashioned.'" "His appearance is like Lebanon. One who enters Lebanon sees a beautiful and precious tree than which there is none higher, nor is any like it found, until he sees one yet more beautiful than it and it is wondrous in his eyes — so is the work of the Shekhinah." "A young man like cedars. Which are upon the waters, that his deeds never cease, in the sense of 'They are new every morning' (great is Your faithfulness)."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra is enumerating occurrences of a repeated word in the passage; 'the fifth' and 'the third' (next comment) refer to this count.", 4 "The parenthetical '(great is Your faithfulness)' translates the words רבה אמונתך embedded in the Hebrew, completing the quotation from Lamentations 3:23."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:50.615779187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}